<article>
	<h1><span>Services &amp; Subscriptions Manager: Services</span></h1>

	<ul class="nav">
		<li><a href="#overview">Overview</a></li>
		<li><a href="#column-headers">Column Headers</a></li>
		<li><a href="#toolbar">Toolbar</a></li>
		<li><a href="#sub-menu">Sub-menu Links</a></li>
	</ul>

	<section id="overview">
		<h2><span>Overview</span></h2>

		<p>This screen lists the services members can subscribe to. The list is sorted by category at first.</p>
	</section>
	<section id="column-headers">
		<h2><span>Column Headers</span></h2>

		<p>Click the <strong>Title</strong>, <strong>Category</strong> or <strong>Status</strong> heading to sort
			the list by that column. Click it again to reverse the order.</p>

		<dl>
			<dt>Checkbox</dt>
			<dd>Check this box to select one or more items. To select all items, check the box in the column heading.
				After one or more boxes are checked, click a toolbar button to take an action on the selected item or
				items. The row checkboxes are shown only to users who may edit.</dd>

			<dt>ID</dt>
			<dd>This is a unique identification number for this item assigned automatically by the system.</dd>

			<dt>Title</dt>
			<dd>The service's title. Users who may edit can click it to open the service for editing.</dd>

			<dt>Category</dt>
			<dd>The service's category.</dd>

			<dt>Status</dt>
			<dd><strong>Active</strong> when the service's status is published, otherwise
				<strong>Inactive</strong>.</dd>
		</dl>
	</section>
	<section id="toolbar">
		<h2><span>Toolbar</span></h2>
		<p>At the top right you will see the toolbar.</p>
		<p>The functions are:</p>
		<dl>
			<dt>Options</dt>
			<dd>Opens the Options window where settings such as default parameters or permissions can be edited.
				Shown only to users who may configure the component.</dd>

			<dt>New</dt>
			<dd>Opens the editing screen to create a new service. Shown only to users who may create.</dd>

			<dt>Edit</dt>
			<dd>Opens the editing screen for the selected service. If more than one service is selected, only the
				first one is opened. Shown only to users who may edit.</dd>

			<dt>Delete</dt>
			<dd>Permanently deletes the selected services. Shown only to users who may delete.</dd>

			<dt>Help</dt>
			<dd>Opens this help screen.</dd>
		</dl>
	</section>
	<section id="sub-menu">
		<h2><span>Sub-menu Links</span></h2>
		<p>At the top left, you will see sub-menu options. The links are:</p>
		<dl>
			<dt>Services (this page)</dt>
			<dt>Subscriptions</dt>
		</dl>
	</section>
</article>
